  "result": "`acceptInvitation` in `src/server/services/invitation-service.ts` never looked at `revokedAt`. It only refused invitations that were already accepted or expired. A cancelled invitation still passed both checks, so anyone holding the link got a membership.\n\nI added a check that throws `\"That invitation has been revoked\"` when `revokedAt` is set. It sits before the expiry check and before the \"already a member\" early return. Already-used and expired links are refused as before. I didn't run the tests. The existing test in `tests/services/invitation-service.test.ts` expects a `/revoked/` error for a revoked token, and the new message matches that pattern.\n\nThe accept action calls this function and nothing else reads the invitation by token, so no other path needed the change.",
